            <div xml:id="d652">

                <pb facs="0641" n="629" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg629"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/882a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-06-02T18:00:00-04:00">June 2, 1937—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>216. Please ascertain whether British Government is pursuing endeavors to obtain
                    definite information on Japanese naval plans and, if so, whether they have any
                    hope of obtaining an early decision.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
